==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|stabilise||UK}}

===Etymology===
From {{suffix|en|stable|ize}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|stāʹ-bəl-īz'}} {{IPA|en|/ˈsteɪ.bəlˌaɪz/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-stabilize.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{hyphenation|en|sta|bil|ize}}
* {{rhymes|en|eɪbəlaɪz|s=3}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To make [[stable]].
#: {{ux|en|Jody '''stabilized''' the table by putting a book under the short leg.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To become [[stable]].
#: {{ux|en|The country will '''stabilize''' after the next election ends.}}

